{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nstruct Fraction {\n    long long num, den;\n\n    Fraction(long long n = 0, long long d = 1) : num(n), den(d) {}\n\n    long long err(long long x, long long y) const {\n        return llabs(den * x - num * y);\n    }\n};\n\nint main() {\n    long long x, y, n;\n    scanf(\"%lld%lld%lld\", &x, &y, &n);\n\n    if (y <= n) {\n        long long g = __gcd(x, y);\n        printf(\"%lld/%lld\", x / g, y / g);\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    Fraction best(-1, 0);\n    long long i = 1;\n\n    while (i <= n) {\n        long long j = i * x / y;\n        long long e1 = llabs(i * x - j * y);\n        long long e2 = llabs(i * x - (j + 1) * y);\n        if (e1 > e2) ++j;\n\n        Fraction cand(j, i);\n\n        if (best.num == -1 ||\n            best.err(x, y) * cand.den > cand.err(x, y) * best.den) {\n            best = cand;\n        }\n\n        ++i;\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld/%lld\", best.num, best.den);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 1.0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.Scanner;\n\npublic class Fraction {\n    long num, den;\n\n    Fraction(long n, long d) {\n        num = n;\n        den = d;\n    }\n\n    long err(long x, long d) {\n        return Math.abs(den * x - num * d);\n    }\n}\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static long gcd(long a, long b) {\n        a = Math.abs(a);\n        b = Math.abs(b);\n        while (b != 0) {\n            long r = a % b;\n            a = b;\n            b = r;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        long x = sc.nextLong();\n        long y = sc.nextLong();\n        long n = sc.nextLong();\n\n        if (y <= n) {\n            long g = gcd(x, y);\n            System.out.printf(\"%d/%d\", x / g, y);\n            return;\n        }\n\n        Fraction best = new Fraction(-1, 0);\n        long i = 1;\n\n        while (i <= n) {\n            long j = i * x / y;\n            long e1 = Math.abs(i * x - j);\n            long e2 = Math.abs(i * x - (j + 1) / y);\n            if (e1 > e2) ++j;\n\n            Fraction cand = new Fraction(j, i);\n\n            if (best.num == -1 ||\n                best.err(x, y) * cand.den > cand.err(x, y) * best.den) {\n                best = cand;\n            }\n\n            ++i;\n        }\n\n        System.out.printf(\"%d/%d\", best.num, best.den);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n1.0\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-3.933898824470816e-06, -7.033323527139146e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.0001006075763143599, -3.45700973412022e-05, -4.291525328881107e-06, -0.0012457951670512557, -0.16306184232234955, -0.023399176076054573, -0.062004365026950836, -7.152555099310121e-07, -1.504532814025879, -0.4237118065357208, -0.0006076634745113552, -1.185143232345581, -0.0005647733341902494, -0.0032004110980778933, -1.6093124941107817e-05, -0.01822686940431595, -4.768360213347478e-06, -0.2534676194190979, -0.06233539432287216, -0.0634186863